"RELEASE 1270 CAUSAL DEATH AND FAILURE FEEDBACK"

;"Authored causal explanations for selected existing failures. This module owns
  no hazard, route, creature, inventory, or death state. It only phrases the
  physical cause, prior evidence, partial validity, and decisive state/action
  difference immediately before canonical JIGS-UP handles death/recovery."

<ROUTINE CAUSAL-FAILURE-DRAGON-TRAP ()
    <JIGS-UP "The chain was a sound mechanism used at the wrong moment. The dragon was still watching the trap instead of standing beneath the grille, so its fire reached you before the counterweight could change the room. The grooves and hanging bars told you what the chain could do; they did not make the animal occupy it. The idea was sound. The missing state was the dragon's position beneath the grille.">>

<ROUTINE CAUSAL-FAILURE-DRAGON-WATCH ()
    <JIGS-UP "Nothing mysterious killed you: you remained exposed after the dragon had spent its visible patience. Heat between its teeth and the swelling chest were the warning, while the south passage remained physically open. Investigating the room was not itself wrong; taking one more unprotected action after the warning changed observation into immolation.">>

<ROUTINE CAUSAL-FAILURE-DRAGON-ATTACK ()
    <JIGS-UP "Direct violence was physically possible, but the dragon was unrestrained, already facing you, and able to fill the room with fire before a sword could settle the argument. The weapon was not a parser mistake. The decisive state was that nothing had yet prevented the dragon from answering immediately.">>

<ROUTINE CAUSAL-FAILURE-DRAGON-TOLL-BREACH ()
    <JIGS-UP "The bargain itself worked. What killed you was crossing its one-object boundary while the dragon still controlled the arch. The claw tap and the single allowance were evidence; taking the first piece was sound, while reaching for a second changed paid passage into theft in front of an armed guardian.">>

<ROUTINE CAUSAL-FAILURE-DRAGON-HOARD-THEFT ()
    <JIGS-UP "The treasure was never unguarded merely because you could reach it. The dragon still owned the doorway and its line of fire. TAKE was not the mistake as a parser verb; the decisive physical state was reaching before anything had stopped the guardian from answering.">>

<ROUTINE CAUSAL-FAILURE-DAM-LADDER ()
    <JIGS-UP "The fall was caused by three facts acting together: open sluices made the rungs slick, your carried weight committed both balance and grip, and no fixed handline existed to arrest the slip. The wet ladder had already advertised the first fact. Descending was not inherently wrong; descending overloaded and unarrested was the decisive state.">>

<ROUTINE CAUSAL-FAILURE-DAM-CURRENT ()
    <JIGS-UP "The current, not the cold or a hidden swimming check, killed you. Open sluices removed your footing and there was no fixed line to arrest the downstream pull. Entering the water was a physically meaningful experiment; the missing state was any prepared restraint capable of stopping that current from carrying you away.">>

<ROUTINE CAUSAL-FAILURE-CANYON-LEAP ()
    <JIGS-UP "Gravity did exactly what the canyon rim said it would. Loose shale had already demonstrated the sheer drop, and you stepped beyond the edge with no physical state able to turn a fall into a controlled descent. LEAP was honored rather than parser-blocked; the decisive difference was the absence of anything that could actually arrest the fall.">>
